<http://data.silknow.org/object/47f6d03d-ef88-3c2c-b359-69c0c9b3dbdb/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Table frontal of tapestry weave silk (kesi). Woven with bright coloured silks on a ground of gilt paper thread tinted with water-colour paint. In the centre of the main panel two birds are standing on conventional rockery. Growing from these rocks is a peony and a magnolia tree and another flowering tree. In the centre of the top panel is a white elephant with a vase on its back. Vases of artists implements, books, fungus and bamboo and a stand with a dish of finger citrons can be seen depicted on either side of the central motif. The borders are composed of pairs of peaches alternating with bats and flowers."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/47f6d03d-ef88-3c2c-b359-69c0c9b3dbdb> .

